Pin Connections

Component| Arduino Uno Pin
HC-SR04 Ultrasonic Sensor (TRIG)| D2
HC-SR04 Ultrasonic Sensor (ECHO)| D3
SG90 Servo Motor (Signal)| D5
Active Buzzer (+)| D6
Green LED (+)| D7
Red LED (+)| D8
OLED Display SDA| A4
OLED Display SCL| A5
OLED Display VCC| 5V
OLED Display GND| GND
Ultrasonic Sensor VCC| 5V
Ultrasonic Sensor GND| GND
Servo Motor VCC| 5V*
Servo Motor GND| GND
Buzzer (-)| GND
Green LED (-)| GND (through 220Ω resistor)
Red LED (-)| GND (through 220Ω resistor)

Note

- Connect all VCC pins to the Arduino 5V pin.
- Connect all GND pins to the Arduino GND pin.
- Use a 220Ω resistor in series with each LED.
- For reliable operation, if the servo motor draws too much current, power it from a separate regulated 5V supply and connect the power supply GND to the Arduino GND (common ground).